  "title": "Classical bounds for graph Ramsey numbers",
  "authors": [
    "Juan Pablo Traverso Gianini"
  ],
  "summary": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the classical bounds for graph Ramsey numbers: R(3, 3) = 6 (every graph on six vertices has a triangle or three independent vertices, and the pentagon has neither), the Erdős–Szekeres upper bound R(s, t) ≤ C(s + t − 2, s − 1), and Erdős's lower bound R(k, k) > 2^(k/2) for k ≥ 3, proved by a union bound over the edge sets of graphs on n vertices.",
